course: dictionary
lesson: 3127
title: Electronics
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Electronics are devices that use electricity and tiny parts called chips to work, such as phones, computers and games consoles. «Strong magnets are kept away from bank cards and electronics.» Here, electronics are things that can be damaged by magnets, so they must be devices like phones and computers.
explain: Electronics can also mean the science of designing and making these devices. «Robotics engineers combine mechanical engineering, electronics and coding to build machines» means electronics is one of the skills they need, like coding is.
explain: The clues in a sentence help you. «Electronics that get wet can sometimes be saved if a grown-up knows straight away» tells you that electronics need care and that getting them dry and checked quickly can help.
fact: Electronics means devices that use electricity and tiny parts like chips.
fact: Electronics can also mean the science and technology of designing and making these devices and their circuits.
fact: Electronics is uncountable, so it takes a singular verb: «Electronics is useful.»
fact: In science lessons, pupils build simple circuits with batteries, bulbs and buzzers.
fact: Phrases you may hear include consumer electronics, the electronics shop and recycle electronics.
exercise: «Strong magnets are kept away from bank cards and electronics.» Which of these are electronics? | Pencils and paper | Plants and rocks | *Phones and computers | Bread and milk
exercise: «Electronics that get wet can sometimes be saved if a grown-up knows straight away.» What should you do if electronics get wet? | *Tell a grown-up straight away | Put them in a bag and forget them | Shake them hard | Wait a week before anyone looks
exercise: «Robotics engineers combine mechanical engineering, electronics and coding.» What does electronics mean here? | *The science of designing and making devices | A shop that sells phones | A kind of food | A type of sports game
test: «Jupiter is surrounded by belts of deadly radiation, which can damage spacecraft electronics.» What can damage spacecraft electronics, according to the sentence? | *Deadly radiation | Warm water | Soft music | Gentle breezes
test: Which phrase names a place where electronics are sold? | *the electronics shop | recycle electronics | consumer electronics | strong magnets
exam: «Strong magnets can wipe the strips on bank cards and damage some electronics.» What does this tell you about electronics? | *They can be damaged by strong magnets | They are always made of wood | They make magnets stronger | They are only found in libraries
